    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a1-a9">

                <pb facs="0398" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg340"/>

                <head>Department of foreign relations and government–Section first.</head>
                <p>Taking into consideration that, on account of recent circumstances, the governor
                    and military commander of the State of San Luis Potosi may have ceased to
                    exercise the duties of his office, the President of the republic is pleased to
                    authorize you to take charge of it as soon as you hear of its vacation, and
                    appoints you governor and military commander of the State, requesting you to
                    give notice to the supreme government as soon as you begin your duties, that it
                    may act in the premises.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence, liberty, and reform!
                            <placeName>Santa Rosa</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-09-05">September 5, 1864</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jesus Gonzalez Ortega</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chief of the First Army Corps of the West,
                            Present.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
